Clearly, a reader and writer cannot operate concurrently at the same point of time without synchronization because of the possibility of data races. We thus envision two specialized locks as a part of the locking mechanism: a _read lock_ and a _write lock_ . The read lock allows multiple readers to operate in parallel on a concurrent object. This leads to high-performance implementations by enhancing read parallelism. Given that there are no concurrent writers, there 
